{title: 468 - A Child of the King}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Eb]My Father is rich in houses and lands,
He [Bb]holdeth the wealth of the world in His [Eb]hands!
[Eb]Of rubies and diamonds, of [Ab]silver and gold,
His [Eb]coffers are full, [F7]He has [Eb]riches [Bb7]un[Eb]told.
[Eb]I’m a child of the King, A child of the King:
With Jesus [Ab]my [Eb]Savior, [Ab]I’m a [Eb]child of [Bb7]the [Eb]King.

Refrain:
[Eb]I'm a child of the King,
[Bb]A child [Eb]of the King:
[Eb]With Jesus [Ab]my Savior,
[Eb]I'm [F7]a [Eb]child [Bb7]of [Eb]the King.

Verse 2:
[Eb]My Father's own Son, the Savior of men,
[Bb]Once wandered on earth [Eb]as the poorest of them;
[Eb]But now He is [Ab]pleading our pardon on high,
[Eb]That we [F7]may be [Eb]His when [Bb7]He comes [Eb]by and by.

Verse 3:
[Eb]I once was an outcast stranger on earth,
[Bb]A sinner by choice, [Eb]an alien by birth,
[Eb]But I've been adopted, [Ab]my name's written down,
[Eb]An heir [F7]to a [Eb]mansion, a [Bb7]robe and [Eb]a crown.

Verse 4:
[Eb]A tent or a cottage, why should I care?
[Bb]They're building a palace [Eb]for me over there;
[Eb]Though exiled from home, [Ab]yet still may I sing:
[Eb]All glory [F7]to God, [Eb]I'm a [Bb7]child of [Eb]the King.
